<title>USA: Kennedy-Wilson sells building for $37.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Kennedy-Wilson sells building for $37.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA MONICA, Calif. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kennedy-Wilson Inc Thursday announced the sale of a first trust deed for the World Savings Center, an an office building located in the lake Merritt financial district of Oakland, Calif., for $37.5 million.</p>
<p>The buyer was Prentiss Properties Trust, a real estate investment trust located in Dallas, Texas.</p>
